        <profileDesc>
            <creation/>
            <abstract>
                <p>This text is attested as part of several works circulating under the label 
                    <foreign xml:lang="gez">Zenā nagaromu la-śǝllāse</foreign> (taken from its first phrase).</p>
                <p>It is attested as introduction of <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1300Dersan">Dǝrsāna Śǝllāse</ref> (for example in 
                    <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESum001">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy, ʿUrā Qirqos, UM-001</ref> or <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/EMIP02056">Washington, D.C., Howard University School of Divinity, Tweed Codex 107</ref>), a collection 
                    of homilies for each month followed by c. 60 miracles of the Trinity.
                </p>
                <p>It is also attested in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr62">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 62</ref> as part of a collection of prayers and seven miracles of
                    the 
                    Trinity arranged according to the days of the week (<ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7331SaySelColl">Sayfa Śǝllāse-type collection</ref>), and possibly also in 
                    <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmy015">Gulo Maḵadā, Dabra Māʿṣo Qǝddus Yoḥannǝs, MY-015</ref> as part of <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2296Sayfas">Sayfa Śǝllāse</ref>.</p>
            </abstract>
